# PART 18 – GLOBAL CRUD AND INTERACTION STANDARDS

Every management page must follow the same interaction conventions.

## Create
- Open a modal, drawer or dedicated form page.
- Validate required fields.
- Show inline error messages.
- Prevent duplicate records where applicable.
- Show success toast after successful mock operation.

## View
- Open a complete detail page or drawer.
- Display all relevant fields.
- Show associated records.
- Show history and audit activity.

## Edit
- Prepopulate existing information.
- Validate changed fields.
- Show unsaved changes warning.
- Require confirmation for sensitive updates.

## Delete
- Confirmation dialog.
- Explain the impact.
- Use soft-delete or archive where appropriate.
- Prevent deletion of records with protected dependencies.
- Show audit activity.

## Activate / Deactivate
- Confirmation dialog.
- Show the current status.
- Explain the effect.
- Update the status visually.

## Bulk Actions
Where applicable:
- Select multiple rows.
- Activate.
- Deactivate.
- Export.
- Assign.
- Archive.

Do not implement bulk deletion for financially or legally sensitive records.

## All tables must support
- Search.
- Sorting.
- Filters.
- Pagination.
- Page-size selection.
- Column alignment.
- Empty states.
- Loading skeletons.
- Error states.
- Responsive behaviour.
- Export where appropriate.

Use reusable table components instead of independently designing each table.

